   "source": [
    "## CONCEPT: groupby: one answer for each group\n",
    "\n",
    "- Sometimes we want one answer **for each group**: for each city, for each class.\n",
    "- Idea: **split** the table into groups, **calculate** for each group, **combine** the answers.\n",
    "- Write: `df.groupby(\"city\")[\"maths\"].mean()` = average Maths of each city.\n",
    "- Read it left to right: group by city → take the maths column → take the mean."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### EXAMPLE: Average Maths of each city"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "cell-8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "           maths  english\n",
      "city                     \n",
      "Islamabad  75.25    76.00\n",
      "Karachi    70.50    76.25\n",
      "Lahore     77.00    68.25\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(df.groupby(\"city\")[[\"maths\", \"english\"]].mean())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 37,
   "id": "cell-9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "           science    name\n",
      "city                      \n",
      "Islamabad       88   Usman\n",
      "Karachi         89  Zainab\n",
      "Lahore          95  Hassan\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(df.groupby(\"city\")[[\"science\", \"name\"]].max())     # best Science mark in each city"
   ]
  },
