   "source": [
    "## CONCEPT: More than one answer: agg\n",
    "\n",
    "- `.agg([\"mean\", \"max\"])` gives many answers at once.\n",
    "- You can use several columns: `df.groupby(\"city\")[[\"maths\", \"science\"]].mean()`.\n",
    "- `df[\"city\"].value_counts()` is a quick way to count each value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### EXAMPLE: Many answers at the same time"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "cell-15",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "            mean  min  max\n",
      "city                      \n",
      "Islamabad  75.25   66   85\n",
      "Karachi    70.50   55   92\n",
      "Lahore     77.00   45   95\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(df.groupby(\"city\")[\"maths\"].agg([\"mean\", \"min\", \"max\"]))"
