   "source": [
    "# Hour 2: Merging Tables"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-21",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## CONCEPT: merge: join two tables\n",
    "\n",
    "- Data is often in **different tables**. Here: marks in one table, fees in another.\n",
    "- Both tables have a shared column: `student_id`. It is the **key**.\n",
    "- `pd.merge(left, right, on=\"student_id\")` puts matching rows together.\n",
    "- `how=\"inner\"` (default) keeps only the ids found in **both** tables.\n",
    "- `how=\"left\"` keeps **all** rows of the left table. If there is no match, you get `NaN`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cell-22",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### EXAMPLE: Join students and fees"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 50,
   "id": "cell-23",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "(12, 6) (11, 3)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(df.shape, fees.shape)      # 12 students, 11 fees"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 53,
   "id": "cell-24",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "   student_id    name       city  maths  english  science fee_paid  fee_amount\n",
